\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Capture a guitar chord voicing and pin its diagram to a point in the timeline, without leaving REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Select an empty item, run this action, and build the voicing by clicking a fretboard grid. The plugin renders a chord diagram into the project folder and attaches it to the item, where it displays in the arrange view and scales as the item is resized.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 HOW TO USE\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Save the project first; the image is stored beside it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Insert an empty item on a track and select exactly one.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Run this action. A window opens with a fretboard grid.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Type the chord as a string \u8212- x32010, or 10-12-12-11-10-10 above the ninth fret \u8212- and the grid redraws as you type.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Or click a cell to place a finger and click it again to remove it, click above the nut to ring a string open or mute it, and the chord string writes itself.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Drag across the strings at a fret to lay a barre over them, as far as the finger reaches \u8212- all six or only two. Click the bar to take it away. A barre is only ever drawn because you drew it, and laying one moves no finger you have already placed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Type a name. It is drawn as the diagram's title and becomes the item's name, so the chord is findable in the Media Item Manager.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} The first fret box says where the top of the grid sits. It fills itself in; change it to frame the chord where you think of it, and press Auto to hand the choice back.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Press Apply to write the diagram to the item, or Cancel or Escape to back out and leave the item exactly as it was.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Run it again on the same item to edit the chord: the voicing is stored on the item, so it comes back already on the grid, and copying the item copies the chord with it.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A barre cannot be written in a chord string, so retyping the text of a chord that has one keeps it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 IF A DIAGRAM DISAPPEARS, it repairs itself. Opening this action on a chord whose image file has gone rebuilds it before the window opens, and you should never notice. If a whole folder of them has gone \u8212- a project copied to another machine without it, or the images tidied away \u8212- run the action "Chord Diagram: regenerate missing diagrams", which rebuilds every one of them in the project and says how many it did.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 IF SOMETHING GOES WRONG, run the action "Chord Diagram: copy diagnostics". It puts a plain-text report on your clipboard \u8212- versions, paths, what is selected and the last error this action showed \u8212- for pasting into a message.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires REAPER 6.44 or newer, js_ReaScriptAPI and ReaImGui 0.9 or newer.\par}
}
